. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. 
.         
.         /*
>         We use plh0308_v2 ("Best if man and woman work the same amount so the
> y can share the responsibility") as an attitudinal measure of gender equality
>  (H4).
>         Here: we want to test if support for gender equality due to having a 
> daughter is higher for men as compared to women.
>         Analysis: We estimate the ATET of having a daughter based on two psma
> tch models (matched on several covariates), one for men and one for women.
>                 Since we cannot directly estimate this in one model, we have 
> to calculate the mean difference in effects between both models by hand. 
>         */
.         
.         eststo m1: teffects psmatch (gender_sharework) (daughter age i.edu i.
> emplstat i.pgfamstd n_children6 hhinc east, probit) if female==0, atet 

Treatment-effects estimation                   Number of obs      =        381
Estimator      : propensity-score matching     Matches: requested =          1
Outcome model  : matching                                     min =          1
Treatment model: probit                                       max =          1
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |              AI robust
gender_sha~k | Coefficient  std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
ATET         |
    daughter |
   (1 vs 0)  |  -.2930403   .2843446    -1.03   0.303    -.8503454    .2642648
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.         eststo m2: teffects psmatch (gender_sharework) (daughter age i.edu i.
> emplstat i.pgfamstd n_children6 hhinc east, probit) if female==1, atet 

Treatment-effects estimation                   Number of obs      =        469
Estimator      : propensity-score matching     Matches: requested =          1
